title: NPR Conference
subtitle: The NPR chooses their stance about Lanckorona...
view-if: lanckorona_pact == 1
on-arrival: npr_leader = 'Vacant'
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true
face-image: img/npr.webp

= NPR Conference

The PSL-P and ZLN has made a pact strengthening their political alliance dubbed as the "Lanckorona Pact" and their parliamentary cooperation dubbed as the "Chjena-Piast". Since the PSL-P was a close partner to the NPR, Now, the party holds a conference to decide their stance on the pact.

During the conference, Jankowski, steps down as party chairman to assume the vice-chair position, the conference will now also elect a new leader.

- @no_chj_pslp: The party elects rejects the Chjeno-Piast.
- @indecisive: The party remains indecisive in their stance.
- @yes_chj_pslp: The party supports the Chjeno-Piast.

@yes_chj_pslp
view-if: npr_relation <= 40
on-arrival: npr_leader = "Wachowiak"; npr_relation -= 15; bourgeoisie_npr += 5; npr_lanckorona = 1
face-image: img/portraits/WachowiakStanisław.jpg

Stanisław Wachowiak, a conservative and Christian democratic figure in the party has been selected as the chairman of the NPR. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Jankowski, and will be more aligned with the ZLN.

@indecisive
view-if: npr_relation > 40 and npr_relation < 70
on-arrival: npr_leader = "Popiel and Chądzyński"; npr_relation -= 5
face-image: img/portraits/NPR_1923_Leader.png

Karol Popiel, a Christian democrat and Adam Chądzyński, a left-wing nationalist had been both selected as the chairman of the NPR, they represent the party's balanced approach to the left and right.

They remain indecisive about the Chjeno-Piast due to their conflicting ideas and the NPR's eagerness of parliamentary balance between the left and right.

@no_chj_pslp
view-if: npr_relation >= 70
on-arrival: npr_leader = "Popiel and Chądzyński"; workers_npr += 5; npr_lanckorona = -1
face-image: img/portraits/NPR_1923_Leader.png

Karol Popiel, a Christian democrat and Adam Chądzyński, a left-wing nationalist had been both selected as the chairman of the NPR, they represent the party's balanced approach to the left and right.

The NPR isn't reluctant in being part of the left-wing opposition if a Chjeno-Piast coalition were to happen, they closely align their beliefs with us while remaining true to their balanced approach.

They reject the Chjeno-Piast.
